Z||000000||BUDDY||06-26-2001||08:59 PM||||I've got an '86 2m4.  The engine began making noise (not bad) so I hooked up an oil pressure gauge to the sensor port and didn't have much oil pressure.  I pulled the oil pan to check the oil pump and while doing so decided to check the connecting rod to crank journal clearance.  #1, 3, & 4 cylinders are around 0.007 - 0.008.  #2 cylinder is 0.011. Does anyone know the tolerance for this clearance.  I have't pulled the oil pump yet.  Once I heal up from pulling the oil pan, I'll pull the oil pump and check it.   <P>------------------<BR>BUDDY||||reg||9
Z||000001||88formula||06-26-2001||09:10 PM||||Main journal oil clearance is .0005 to .0022. Connecting rod oil journal clearance is .0005 to .0026.<P>What method did you use to check your clearances? If you really have .011 than the bearings would look really bad.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
